 - [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
 - [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
 - [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the resolution outcome.
 - [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
-- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves a visit's review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity, the adopted revision, and all contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: When a visit's first valid submission is accepted, the system SHALL store it as the visit's revision 1 and mark that revision as the visit's current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When an accepted submission names the visit's current revision as its base revision, the system SHALL store the payload as a new revision and make that revision the visit's current revision without marking review work unresolved.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When an accepted submission names a base revision other than the visit's current revision, the system SHALL retain the payload as a competing revision and mark the visit unresolved.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: While a visit is unresolved, when any further valid submission is accepted for that visit, the system SHALL retain it as an additional competing revision and leave the visit unresolved.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a coordinator adopts one of a visit's competing revisions, the system SHALL make the adopted revision the visit's current revision, clear the visit's unresolved state, and retain every competing submission.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a caller retrieves an unresolved visit, the system SHALL return no current payload and SHALL return every competing revision with its revision number, author, receipt time, and payload.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a caller retrieves a resolved visit, the system SHALL return the current revision's payload with its revision number and author.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When any submission, resolution, or later edit is stored for a visit, the system SHALL preserve every previously retained submission for that visit unchanged.
